  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Defend as a team",
  "description": "Play 8 v 8 on half a pitch with a big goal and a keeper. The coach stands in the centre circle with balls and starts every attack with a pass to blue. Blue attack and try to score. Offside applies.\n\nRed defend in two lines of four. If red win the ball they score by playing it back to the coach, making three passes in a row, or dribbling the ball under control over the halfway line.\n\nStop the game when needed and show the distances within and between the lines. Swap roles after 8–10 minutes. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keep good distances within and between the lines – no big gaps to play through."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The nearest player presses, the others shift with the ball and cover."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Step up together when the ball is played backwards or out wide."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Keeper and back line talk all the time – who takes whom, when do we step up?"
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "game",
  "difficulty": 4,
